[size=3][b]FAQ:
[/b][/size][size=2]Q: Why does the extension integrate with Fluffy to Install Mods?
A: Here are a few details as to why this choice was made:
[list]
[*][size=2]Most mod authors package their mods for Fluffy. Rather than "pushing against" the community and trying to create custom solutions, it seems better for the Vortex user to integrate with Fluffy and allow it to handle mod variants and install patterns. This avoids a lot of edge case install failures and avoids resorting to a less polished user experience. [/size]
[*][size=2]A secondary requirement of using Fluffy properly is keeping mods in zip files. The Vortex extension must re-zip the mod files during installation to do this. This is usually very fast, but could take a short time for large file-size mods, depending on your PC performance.[/size][/size]
[/list]

